      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. it sounds like even a tiny flaw in the material can totally change the acoustic profile. do those microscopic disturbances ever act in a way that feels almost... reactive? like, if a player tries to force a very pure, stable tone, do those anomalous partials seem to behave in a way that's intentionally disruptive or even quite troublesome for the performer?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
